  "conclusions": [
    "The selected development policy uses min_observations=8, max_probe_bytes=64 and symmetric 256:1/1:256 likelihood thresholds.",
    "On the five-file Pizza&Chili pseudo-real holdout, sequential routing averages 3.5239 bpb versus 3.5553 for the fixed 256-byte router and 3.5213 for always-neural.",
    "Sequential routing decides after 22.4 bytes on average and correctly rejects neural on DNA as well as repetition/random controls.",
    "On self-v2 it activates neural at byte 8 and remains within about 0.0085 bpb of always-neural on the same 4096-byte reporting slice.",
    "A false-positive neural activation remains on proteins-mut, so confidence routing is substantially improved but not a solved universal routing policy.",
    "zlib and zstd still beat POLLICINO on average on this holdout; the result is routing efficiency and specialization control, not universal compression superiority."
  ],
